course: dictionary
lesson: 7569
title: A presentation can be a talk, a prize-giving or neat work
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. «Presentation» is one of them. Look at the words around it to find out which meaning fits best.
explain: «Useful feedback says what was good and why, for example "Your facts about lava were really clear".» Here a presentation is a talk to a group, where someone shows and explains facts about lava. That is the first meaning.
explain: «Handwriting (presentation) and composition (what is written and how well) are different skills and are marked separately.» Here presentation means how neat the work looks, like handwriting and underlined titles. The brackets tell you the word is being explained.
explain: «Jayden wanted a 16 game for his tenth birthday, so he did what any serious person would do: he made a five-page presentation.» Jayden's five pages were made to show and explain why he should get the game. Try each meaning in the sentence and keep the one that fits.
fact: A presentation can be a talk to a group that shows or explains something, often with slides or pictures.
fact: A presentation can also be the giving of something to someone in a ceremony, such as the presentation of prizes.
fact: Presentation can also mean the way something looks or is set out, such as neat presentation in your book.
fact: You can give a presentation, do a presentation, or go to a presentation evening.
fact: Slang: «That presentation ate» is Gen Z slang meaning it was excellent.
exercise: A pupil talks to the class about volcanoes and uses slides. What is this called? | A holiday | *A presentation | A prize | Snacks
exercise: «The presentation of prizes was held at the sports day.» What does presentation mean here? | *Giving something to someone in a ceremony | Neat handwriting | A talk with slides | A shop window
exercise: The teacher marks your neat presentation with a tick. What does presentation mean? | A talk to the class | A party for your friends | *The way the work looks and is set out | A prize for speaking
test: Which phrase means you are giving a talk to a group? | Eat a presentation | Wear a presentation | *Give a presentation | Lose a presentation
test: «Handwriting (presentation) and composition are marked separately.» What does presentation mean in this sentence? | A ceremony with prizes | A type of slide | A talk to a group | *How neat the work looks
exam: In «That presentation ate», what does ate mean? | Burnt to a crisp | Too long and boring | *Excellent | Finished every bit of it
